From 8969b05068aa586c85abf51bb7737bb2a8f67bc6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:13:44 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 38/97] scripting: layers, effects, sounds and the scene as
 SceneScript has them

Scripts reach every layer the way Wallpaper Engine documents the API:

- thisScene.getLayer (n) is the n-th layer of the scene (not an object
  id), and every type is a layer: images, texts, particles, sounds and
  groups (a group or camera object is a CGroup now). One JS object per
  layer, so getLayer ('a') === getLayer ('a') and what a script stores
  on a layer stays. getLayerCount, enumerateLayers, getLayerIndex and
  sortLayer (the draw order follows) exist; createLayer is undefined
  and destroyLayer false (not supported).
- ILayer: id, solid (scene.json, default true), size, getParent,
  getChildren, getEffect (name or index) / getEffectCount, and
  getTextureAnimation. A name the layer doesn't have is kept on it.
  `pointsize` is pointSize.
- IEffect: name, and `visible` written live (E41's chain). Every effect
  is built when the scene's scripts call getEffect, so one hidden at
  load can be shown. The material calls are no-ops.
- ITextureAnimation: frameCount, duration, rate, play/pause/stop,
  isPlaying, getFrame/setFrame and join. A call that changes it takes
  the layer off the shared clock onto its own, as WE's docs say.
- ISoundLayer: a sound object is scriptable: volume (live), play ()
  (only if not running; resumes a pause; starts a startsilent sound),
  stop () (rewinds; only play () restarts it), pause (), isPlaying ().
- IScene's properties are writable, clearenabled no longer returns
  bloom, skylightcolor no longer returns the ambient colour, and the
  bloom strength/threshold are floats. Scripts on general's bloom
  values run (thisLayer = the bloom image), and bloom is built for one.
- engine.canvasSize, screenResolution (the scene's size: the core
  doesn't know the output's), userProperties (live, colours as Vec3),
  isDesktopDevice/isMobileDevice/isWallpaper/isScreensaver/
  isRunningInEditor/isPortrait/isLandscape, registerAsset,
  isObjectValid; openUserShortcut returns false.
- applyUserProperties gets the changed user properties on every change,
  after the first call with all of them.
- Text-layer scripts: thisLayer is the real layer (its text is the
  layer's text value), init gets the text and its return is adopted,
  a combo's default is its first option, script properties are read
  live, init and applyUserProperties run with the property scripts',
  the script runs while its layer is hidden or has no font, and the
  events reach it too. A text another layer's script writes is drawn.
- console.log separates its arguments with spaces.

Origin: ours
Why: most scripted scenes call these (docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B10: S15, S16, S19, S20, S24-S27, S29-S32, S37)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01288H8XbjUdhpEVfhFbe7bj
